# Real secrets. The glob matters: a bare `.env` does NOT cover `.env.bak`,
# `.env.local`, `.env.production` or any other suffixed copy, so a backup made
# while editing config would be committable. The negation keeps the documented
# template tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.exe
# Corporate TLS inspection root CA — machine-specific, never commit
infra/*.pem
dist/
bin/
services/data-ingestion/bin/
coverage.out
vendor/
# Compiled binaries that may land in the module root
services/data-ingestion/data-*
services/data-analyzer/fundamental-analysis
services/data-analyzer/technical-analysis

*.pem
# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Go build outputs left in the package directory. macro-analysis was committed
# (13 MB) because it was the one sibling missing from the list above —
# fundamental-analysis and technical-analysis were already ignored. Listed by
# name AND by pattern so the next binary does not slip through the same gap.
services/data-analyzer/macro-analysis
services/data-analyzer/momentum-*
services/data-ingestion/data-*
services/*/bin/
